# Redis / asynq

See `docs/REDIS.md` for configuration and key-space conventions.

## Job queues

- Queue client/server in `internal/infrastructure/queue/asynq`.
- **Notification jobs** (meeting created/updated/cancelled) enqueued from application-layer commands → processed by `platform/meeting_notifier` → Telegram bot send.
- Worker runs in-process alongside the HTTP server (`cmd/server`).

## Reminder scheduler

- `platform/reminder_scheduler` runs a **Redis-leader-locked tick loop** so only one replica fires reminders when the binary is scaled horizontally.
- Lock key and TTL configured via env — see `docs/REDIS.md`.

## Rules

- Enqueue from commands only; never from query handlers (CQRS).
- Task type constants live in the queue package — do not scatter magic strings across layers.
- Keep task payloads small (IDs only); workers fetch full data from Postgres.
